e/godot/pull/106180.patch","merged_at":"2025-05-20T16:39:44Z"},"body":"This commit improves the behavior of 2D camera limits for edge cases when the limits are smaller than the screen rect.\r\n\r\nPresently the RIGHT and TOP limit take precedence simply because they happened to be coded to apply second. This effectively means the part of the scene within the desired limit bounds (typically the focus) is placed in the top right corner of the viewport.\r\nThis change adjusts behavior to split the difference in cases where both the LEFT/RIGHT or TOP/BOTTOM limits both apply  resulting in the target area being placed in the center of the viewport which is more natural and expected. \r\n\r\nThere's no change in the typical case where the camera limits are larger than the screen rect.\r\n\r\nAdjusted the if-else chain so there's no performance cost for this change (same number of tests are performed).\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106180/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused